                                        "entry_id": "e8d6a727-cea4-38ee-9383-012735430320",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A railroad passenger car that is either privately owned or used privately, or both."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19a71653-fa52-4d0b-9024-d8db91c44e69",
                                                "sense_id": "f765ad70-31cd-37a3-b6a5-6981c7da9469",
                                                "text": "In the days before televised press conferences, or debates between Presidential contenders, the railroads carried the politicians to the people. Here, President Truman addresses a crowd from the verandah of his private car, at Sacramento during the 1952 campaign."
